WEBVTT

00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:10.481
This video shows how to set up an academic year and its terms on your phone. You will add a new year, make it the current one, and then add a term inside it.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:21.235
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Management, and then choose Sessions. Each academic year is shown as a card on this page.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.936
Tap Add Academic Year. A form opens where you describe the new year.

00:00:32.848 --> 00:00:46.504
Type a name for the year, for example 2027-2028, and then enter its start date and its end date. Tap Create. A message confirms it, and the new year appears as a card.

00:00:54.617 --> 00:01:11.129
To make this the active year, tap the three dots on its card and choose Set as current year. The box that opens tells you if the year has not started yet. Tap Set as Current to confirm. From then on, the rest of the app works with this year.

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:31.720
The year has no terms yet, so tap Add terms on its card. A window opens with the timeline of this year. Terms divide the year into parts, such as Term 1 and Term 2.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:50.012
Tap Add Term. The app creates Term 1 for you, starting on the first day of the year. Change its end date, and wait a moment. The page saves by itself and shows that all changes are saved. Repeat this for every term of the year.

00:01:56.107 --> 00:02:05.155
Your academic year and its first term are ready. You can now create classes, schedule exams and generate fees for this year.
